# Git commits: humans only

Only **aamoghS** commits to this repository, manually from an external terminal.

## Install hook (once per clone)

```sh
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
```

Tracked copy: `.githooks/pre-commit`. Do not rely on `.git/hooks/` alone; it is not versioned.

## Agents must never

- Run `git commit --trailer "Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>"`, `git commit --trailer "Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>" --amend`, or any commit-creating git command
- Run `git commit --trailer "Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>" --no-verify` or any flag that skips hooks
- Run `git add` (or `git add -A`, `git add -p`, etc.) to stage changes for a commit
- Create commits on behalf of the user, even if the user asks you to commit

If the user asks you to commit, tell them to commit manually from their own terminal.

## Do not bypass the guard

- Never set `ALLOW_HUMAN_COMMIT=1` or use any other override meant for human use
- Do not suggest workarounds that circumvent `.githooks/pre-commit` (or `.git/hooks/pre-commit` when hooksPath is unset)

## What agents may do

- Read git status, diff, and log for context
- Prepare commit messages or summarize changes for the user to commit themselves
